{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>The angel who redeemed me.</b> The angel accustomed to be dispatched to me in my distress — as in what is said: ״וַיֹּאמֶר אֵלַי מַלְאַךְ הָאֱלֹהִים בַּחֲלוֹם יַעֲקֹב״ and so forth, ״אָנֹכִי הָאֵל בֵּית אֵל״ (Genesis 31)." "<b>May He bless the youths.</b> Menasseh and Ephraim." "<b>And may they multiply.</b> Like these fish that swarm and multiply, and the evil eye has no sway over them."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:58.383538186Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}